+\subsection{Fixed-body RANS extension}
+\label{sec:rans-methodology}
+
+The fixed NACA~0012 experiment is repeated at $M_\infty=0.1$, $\alpha=6^\circ$, and $Re_c=6\times10^6$ with Spalart--Allmaras (SA) and shear-stress-transport (SST) closures~\cite{SpalartAllmaras1994,Menter1994}. The purpose is to assess remeshing-induced transients about a nominally steady viscous state, not a moving-body response or turbulence-model validation. Both closures use the same hybrid mesh: 29,956 vertices, 14,070 quadrilaterals, and 31,339 triangles, with 370 surface vertices and a farfield at $100c$. The first off-wall spacing is approximately $5\times10^{-6}c$; the quadrilateral region extends to about $0.053c$. The reported surface values reach $y^+\simeq\RansMaxYplus$, so near-wall resolution is not assumed converged from the first spacing alone.
+
+Mean-flow fluxes use HLLC with MUSCL reconstruction and a Venkatakrishnan limiter. Turbulence convection uses scalar upwinding without MUSCL reconstruction. The second-order transfer label therefore does not describe the order of every term in the receiving RANS discretization. BDF2 uses $\Delta t=10^{-3}$, 50 inner iterations per physical step, CFL~6, and FGMRES with ILU preconditioning and a 60-iteration linear limit. Here the velocity reference is the freestream sound speed: $a_\infty=1$ and $U_\infty=0.1$, unlike the Euler normalization in Sec.~\ref{sec:naca-fixed-methodology}. The 400-step comparison spans only $tU_\infty/c=0.04$. Each closure has its own 800-step no-transfer reference, initialized with the same steady and startup histories as its perturbed calculations. References are subtracted at matching steps; their startup relaxation is not treated as statistical noise.
+
+The repeated-transfer comparison uses NN2 and limited GP2, each with two prescribed random sequences and a ten-step event interval. Surface vertices and the 12,233 vertices within wall distance $d_w<0.01c$ remain fixed. The displacement band extends to $20c$, with SF4 and a specified quality floor of 0.2. These settings establish a protected inner region, not that the entire quadrilateral layer is unchanged. Both methods receive the same sequence for each seed. In the recorded window, 39 mesh replacements are followed by physical evolution; an additional terminal history-pair export has no following force sample and is excluded from the corresponding transfer summary. An independently converged solution on the first displaced mesh provides a separate native-mesh comparison. One-event GP2 calculations use bands $[0.05,0.10]c$, $[0.10,0.15]c$, and $[0.20,0.25]c$, with selected SF2 and longer-window cases.
+
+Density, momentum, energy, and both histories of the turbulence state are transferred. The recorded turbulence inventories are density-weighted $\widetilde\nu$ for SA and $k,\omega$ for SST. SST output is clipped to the implemented primitive-variable floors $k\geq10^{-10}$ and $\omega\geq10^{-4}$; this post-pass is absent in the SA runs. Wall distance and derived eddy viscosity are recomputed by the solver. No separate NN2--GC comparison or RANS mixed-history experiment is supplied. The results therefore concern the returned NN2 and GP2 pipelines, including their post-processing, rather than every nominal transfer order or the isolated contribution of turbulence-history error.
+
+Total loads are taken from the force histories. Pressure and friction contributions are additionally integrated from the exported surface fields using the same quadrature for case and reference. These differences resolve changes hidden by the six-decimal force-breakdown output, but the underlying surface fields remain single precision. Surface records duplicated at identical physical steps are counted once. The corresponding script, precision limitations, event accounting, and supporting diagnostics are documented in Appendix~\ref{app:rans-details}.
