+The RANS archive provides complete reduced force histories and selected surface distributions, but not the case-level meshes, restart vectors, solver sources, or inner-residual histories. Fifty inner iterations is an iteration budget, not evidence that the physical-step error lies below each measured difference. A selected tightened-inner-iteration and time-step check at fixed physical remeshing times is needed before small method differences are interpreted as resolved accuracy differences. Exact closure variants, freestream turbulence values, thermal wall conditions, the coordinate-based displacement mask, and software version should accompany the configuration archive. These are bounded verification and reporting requirements for this fixed-body study, not a requirement to add moving-body simulations.
+
 \section{Data provenance and automated checks}
 \label{app:automated-postprocessing}
 
-All pre-existing input and generated CSV files retain their names, locations, and numerical contents. Figures and tables read these files through \texttt{pgfplots} and \texttt{pgfplotstable}. The static-data builder recomputes fitted and consecutive orders from the supplied errors; the manuscript build tracks CSV dependencies. The additional audit script checks tabulated ratios, fits, citation keys, and preservation of the original CSV hashes. It does not rerun the flow solver.
-
-The static error/conservation CSVs are the available numerical inputs. The Riemann and NACA CSVs in this package are summaries transcribed from the supplied study reports, not replacements for the original full-precision run outputs named there. The reports are retained unchanged for provenance. The residual-summary CSV includes normalized cosine values slightly above one; these invalid angular diagnostics are preserved in the input but omitted from the numerical assessment pending recomputation. No continuous force history, pressure-shell history, state vector, or residual vector is reconstructed from isolated summary values. The editorial audit records unresolved settings, tracker inconsistencies, and diagnostics requiring original data; these must be resolved before a fully reproducible journal submission.
-
+The 39 pre-existing input/generated CSVs and 14 RANS source CSVs retain their names, relative locations, and contents. Figures and tables use \texttt{pgfplots} and \texttt{pgfplotstable}; the build tracks their dependencies. The static builder recomputes convergence orders. The RANS builder creates derived views, rejects conflicting duplicate physical keys, removes only exact repeated snapshots, aligns event windows, and recomputes descriptive statistics. Its hash manifest distinguishes original data from derived products and detects later intentional source updates. Neither builder runs CFD.
+
+The original reports are retained. Earlier Riemann/Euler NACA CSVs contain report-transcribed summaries; the new RANS files contain reduced post-processing exports, including actual sampled force histories. Continuous curves are drawn only where time samples exist. Report-only floor statistics are labeled separately. The earlier residual-summary CSV's cosines above one remain preserved but excluded from validation. The accompanying scientific assessment records the remaining source/precision and solver-control limitations and the bibliographic additions. Reproduction from these reduced data is not a substitute for archiving the configurations, meshes, restart states, and extraction scripts required to reproduce the simulations themselves.
